When haven't we had frequent updates? ;)

v1-0-10-branch was created for the case we would need to release
1.0.10a driver, which should include basically only critical fixes,
just like 2.6.x.y stable kernel tree.

If you look at the patches yesterday closely, you'll notice that the
most of changes are only systematic replacements and clean-ups.  There
are no big structural changes which may break something severely.
(If you allow me to break, I'll happily apply other dozen of patches.
 Until yesterday, I had 5 branches on my local CVS repository...)

The other additional patches like the new support of PM or PnP BIOS
are forward-porting of old pending patches.

Also, there is no branch for libs, utils, and others.

